 <FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" ><B>My main concern...</b></font>
<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >is the lack of options. This game seems like it might be short on variety. Perhaps they are just marketing it wrong. If they marketed it as a massively multiplayer online space sim, it would appeal to the space sim market and it could very well be successful. But the fact they are marketing it as an MMORPG... well, MMORPG players have come to expect lots of variety in skills, classes, races or what have you. Some may be turned off by the apparent lack of options.<br>
<br>
Then again there is not a lot of info about this game yet, and they have been working on it for 4 years, so hopefully they have other stuff up their sleeves to keep it interesting.<br>
<br>
As for other sci-fi MMORPGs, Anarchy Online might be fun. UO2 is kinda sci-fi fantasy hybrid, and of course there are planetside and SWO (whitefox will call me a verant-lover now that I mentioned both planetside and SWO in one sentence hehe)<br>
<br>
Seems we have a lot of options coming. I hope a few of them are as good as the hype surrounding them...</font></p>

